---
/**
 * FAQ
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Native <details>/<summary>: keyboard accessible, works with JavaScript
 * disabled, and the answers are real text in the HTML — required both for
 * crawlability and because FAQPage structured data may only describe content
 * that is visible on the page.
 *
 * The small script adds smooth exclusive-open behaviour and nothing else.
 */
import SectionHeader from './SectionHeader.astro';
import { project } from '../data/project';
import { interpolate } from '../utils/format';
import { faqReplacements, hasUnfilledPlaceholder } from '../utils/structuredData';

/*
 * The token map and the placeholder guard are shared with the FAQPage
 * structured data, so the page and the markup describe exactly the same set.
 * An answer with an unfilled [PLACEHOLDER] is dropped rather than printed — a
 * bracket is not an answer.
 */
const items = project.faq
  .map((item) => ({
    question: interpolate(item.question, faqReplacements),
    answer: interpolate(item.answer, faqReplacements),
  }))
  .filter((item) => !hasUnfilledPlaceholder(item.answer));
---

<section class="section section--alt" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="FAQ" title="Frequently Asked Questions" id="faq-title" />

    <div class="faq" data-faq>
      {
        items.map((item, i) => (
          <details class="faq__item" name="faq" open={i === 0}>
            <summary class="faq__q">
              <span>{item.question}</span>
              <span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true" />
            </summary>
            <div class="faq__a">
              <p>{item.answer}</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    max-width: 62rem;
  }

  .faq__item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line);
  }

  .faq__q {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--sp-4);
    padding-block: var(--sp-4);
    min-height: 48px;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--c-ink);
    transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }

  .faq__q::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq__q:hover {
    color: var(--c-accent-ink);
  }

  .faq__q:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--c-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .faq__icon {
    position: relative;
    flex: none;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    margin-top: 0.45em;
  }

  .faq__icon::before,
  .faq__icon::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    background: var(--c-accent);
    transition: transform var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }

  .faq__icon::before {
    inset: 6px 0 auto 0;
    height: 1.5px;
  }

  .faq__icon::after {
    inset: 0 6px 0 auto;
    width: 1.5px;
  }

  .faq__item[open] .faq__icon::after {
    transform: scaleY(0);
  }

  .faq__a {
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-5);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .faq__a p {
    color: var(--c-ink-2);
  }
</style>

<script>
  /*
   * `name="faq"` gives exclusive accordion behaviour natively in modern
   * browsers. This fallback provides the same behaviour where it is not yet
   * supported. Everything still works with the script absent — the items just
   * open independently.
   */
  const supportsExclusive = 'name' in document.createElement('details');
  if (!supportsExclusive) {
    const group = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDetailsElement>('[data-faq] details');
    group.forEach((item) => {
      item.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
        if (!item.open) return;
        group.forEach((other) => {
          if (other !== item) other.open = false;
        });
      });
    });
  }
</script>
